---
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import { ISSUES_URL, REPO_CONFIGURED } from '../site';

const privacy = url('/privacy/');
const license = url('/license/');
---

<section id="faq" class="section section--alt" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <header class="section-head section-head--center">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h2 id="faq-title">Questions, answered plainly</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Is Krova really free?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes. It is open source under the <a href={license}>MIT License</a>: you can use it, read the code, modify it
          and share it. There is no account to create.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Does it connect to the internet?</summary>
        <p>
          No. Krova makes no network calls, collects no telemetry and needs no account. If you want to check for
          yourself, block it in your firewall or watch it with your system’s network monitor. Details are on the
          <a href={privacy}>privacy page</a>.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Where are my layouts and settings stored?</summary>
        <p>
          In a single <code>config.json</code> file in your user application-data folder. It holds your settings and
          each monitor’s layouts. Window titles are never logged or stored.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What happens when I unplug and reconnect a monitor?</summary>
        <p>
          Each monitor’s layouts are saved against its hardware identity, so they come back when it does. Where a
          monitor doesn’t report a usable identity, Krova falls back to its device path, then to its resolution and
          position.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Does it replace Windows Snap or clash with it?</summary>
        <p>
          No. Windows’ own Snap Assist stays on. Krova only acts while you hold its activation key, so the two don’t
          fight each other.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Why won’t it move one of my windows on Windows?</summary>
        <p>
          Windows of apps running as administrator (elevated) are skipped. Minimized and full-screen windows are
          skipped as well.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Why does macOS ask for Accessibility permission?</summary>
        <p>
          macOS only lets an app move and resize other apps’ windows once you allow it under System Settings, Privacy
          &amp; Security, Accessibility. Without that permission Krova can’t snap windows.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I use my keyboard instead of dragging?</summary>
        <p>
          Not yet. Layouts you can trigger from the keyboard are planned for v0.2. In v0.1 you snap by dragging a
          window while holding the activation key.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is there a Linux version?</summary>
        <p>No. Krova supports Windows 10/11 and macOS 13 or later only.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>When can I download it?</summary>
        <p>
          Krova is at version 0.1 and has not been released yet. The <a href="#download">download section</a> will list
          the installers once they exist.{' '}
          {
            REPO_CONFIGURED && (
              <Fragment>
                Found a problem or have an idea? <a href={ISSUES_URL}>Open an issue</a>.
              </Fragment>
            )
          }
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-s);
    min-height: 3.5rem;
    padding-block: var(--space-xs);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    font-weight: 650;
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  summary::after {
    content: '';
    flex: none;
    width: 0.6rem;
    height: 0.6rem;
    margin-right: 0.3rem;
    border-right: 2px solid currentColor;
    border-bottom: 2px solid currentColor;
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    transition: transform var(--dur) var(--ease-out);
  }

  details[open] > summary::after {
    transform: rotate(-135deg);
  }

  summary:focus-visible {
    outline-offset: 0;
  }

  details p {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-m);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
